<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FTL>
	<mod:findName type="event" name="NEMESIS_DROPPOINT">
		<mod-append:preventQuest/>
		<mod-append:runFromFleet closest="false"/>
		<mod-append:preventBossFleet forever="true"/>
		<mod-append:beaconType id="leah_nemesis_droppoint" global="true">
			<color r="255" g="200" b="0" a="1.0"/>
			<unvisitedTooltip>This is the location of Your Nemesis.</unvisitedTooltip>
			<visitedTooltip>Explored location. Nothing left of interest.</visitedTooltip>
		</mod-append:beaconType>
		<mod-append:choice req="LIST_CREW_LEAH" max_group="666" hidden="true" blue="true">
			<text>(Leah) Use Leah to hail the ship.</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH"/>
		</mod-append:choice>
	</mod:findName>
	
	<mod:findName type="event" name="NEMESIS_FIRST">
		<mod-append:choice req="LEAH_LIST_BEAMS_SMALL" hidden="true" blue="true">
			<text>(Beam Weapon) Show her your Beam weapon.</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_BEAM_SMALL"/>
		</mod-append:choice>
		<mod-append:choice req="LEAH_LIST_BEAMS_MEDIUM" hidden="true" blue="true">
			<text>(Large Beam Weapon) Show her your large Beam weapon.</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_BEAM_MEDIUM"/>
		</mod-append:choice>
		<mod-append:choice req="LEAH_LIST_BEAMS_BIG" hidden="true" blue="true">
			<text>(Gigantic Beam Weapon) Show her your gigantic Beam weapon.</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_BEAM_BIG"/>
		</mod-append:choice>
		<mod-append:choice req="leah_prof_nemesis_leah_quest_completed" hidden="true" blue="true">
			<text>(Your Nemesis's Appreciation) Your computer beeps upon hearing her voice.</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_META"/>
		</mod-append:choice>
	</mod:findName>
	
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_BEAM_SMALL">
		<text>"What? Trying to- a Beam! But it's so small. Beyatch, did you really think something like that would impress me?" Though her words say otherwise, she is clearly excited.

"As the infamous BEAM MASTER, of course I'd be the firstmost expert on them! If you wanted to impress me, you'd need something way more powerful, like the Glaive or the Voulge!
Here, let me just- I know a guy who's cousin's mother's knows another guy who's friend's sister knows another guy's brother who knows a Beam dealer." She transfers some coordinates to your ship.

"It's pretty far away, it'll be easier if you meet up with me in each sector. Hold on beyatch, I'll go make the preparations!" Her ship's engines flare up and its FTL Drive activates. "Wait, uh, I forgot I was gonna fight you, beyatch! We'll settle this next time, beyaaaaatcccchhhh-"</text>
		<instantEscape/>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_START"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_BEAM_MEDIUM">
		<text>"What? Trying to- a Beam! Powerful, too! Still not one of the higher-end ones, though. Ah, beyatch, did you really think something like that would impress me?" Though her words say otherwise, she is clearly excited.

"As the infamous BEAM MASTER, of course I'd be the firstmost expert on them! If you wanted to impress me, you'd need something way more powerful, like the Glaive or the Voulge!
Here, let me just- I know a guy who's cousin's mother's knows another guy who's friend's sister knows another guy's brother who knows a Beam dealer." She transfers some coordinates to your ship.

"It's pretty far away, it'll be easier if you meet up with me in each sector. Hold on beyatch, I'll go make the preparations!" Her ship's engines flare up and her FTL Drive activates. "Wait, uh, I forgot I was gonna fight you, beyatch! We'll settle this next time, beyaaaaatcccchhhh-"</text>
		<instantEscape/>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_START"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_BEAM_BIG">
		<text>"What? Trying to- a Beam! Woah, that's a big ass Beam! How'd you get your hands on one of those!?" She is clearly excited.

"I gotta get one of those for myself, beyatch! See, I know a guy who's cousin's mother's knows another guy who's friend's sister knows another guy's brother who knows a Beam dealer. As a fellow Beam aficiando, maybe you've heard of it?" She transfers some coordinates to your ship.

"It's pretty far away, it'll be easier if you meet up with me in each sector. You HAVE TO meet up with me, okay, beyatch? I'll go make the preparations!" Her ship's engines flare up and her FTL Drive activates.</text>
		<instantEscape/>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_START"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SHOW_META">
		<text>"What? Trying to- Oh. Hold on a minute." A moment passes and you see her eyes glaze over lines of words.
"Uh. Huh. Er. Okay. Beyatch, I have been informed of something! No, I won't tell you beyatch! But I have been informed of something! Here are the coordinates to something, come or don't come! Either way, our rivalry will have to wait until next time, beyatch!" She deposits some scrap your way, and then her ship's engines flare up and her FTL Drive activates.</text>
		<instantEscape/>
		<item_modify>
			<item type="scrap" min="31" max="37"/>
		</item_modify>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_START"/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_START">
		<quest event="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY"/>
		<text>You log the coordinates into your ship's computer. Whoever that person was, it may be a good idea to avoid her entirely.</text>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY">
		<quest>
			<nebulaBeacon>true</nebulaBeacon>
			<currentSector>false</currentSector>
			<nextSector>true</nextSector>
			<sectorEight>true</sectorEight>
			<lastStand>true</lastStand>
		</quest>
		<preventQuest/>
		<preventFleet/>
		<preventBossFleet forever="true"/>
		<beaconType id="leah_nemesis_relay" global="true">
			<color r="255" g="200" b="0" a="1.0"/>
			<unvisitedTooltip>This is the location of the coordinates given to you by the "BEAM MASTER".</unvisitedTooltip>
			<visitedTooltip>Explored location. Nothing left of interest.</visitedTooltip>
		</beaconType>
		<text>You've arrived at the coordinates the "BEAM MASTER" gave. You see her ship, along with the remains of another ship, clearly sliced cleanly in two. She hails you.</text>
		<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS"/>
		<variable name="leah_nemesis_leah_quest_relay" op="add" val="1"/>
		<choice hidden="true" req="leah_nemesis_leah_quest_relay" lvl="0" max_lvl="0" blue="false">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"Hey, beyatch! You actually made it! I wasn't sure if you would- ahem! Anyways, here are the coordinates to our next meeting point. Oh, and that ship? Some weirdo tried to get the jump on me, but I showed them! That's why you don't mess with the Beam Master, beyatch!"
"I would totally fight you right now beyatch, but that battle scratched my hull by the teeniest tiniest amount, so our rivalry is on hold for now, beyatch! You get a pass, just for today!" And with that, her ship's FTL Drive activates. With nothing else to do, you scrap the remains of the abandoned ship.</text>
				<instantEscape/>
				<autoReward level="MED">standard</autoReward>
				<quest event="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY"/>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Continue...</text>
					<event/>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
		<choice hidden="true" req="leah_nemesis_leah_quest_relay" lvl="1" max_lvl="1" blue="false">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"Hey, beyatch! There's totally something wrong with these sectors, people keep jumping in and attacking me for no reason. I didn't even provoke them or anything, they just started charging their weapons. Crazy, huh, beyatch? Anyways, here are the coordinates to our next meeting point."
"Again, I would fight you, beyatch, but... You get another pass, okay? Just for today!" And with that, her ship's FTL Drive activates. With nothing else to do, you scrap the remains of the abandoned ship.</text>
				<instantEscape/>
				<autoReward level="MED">standard</autoReward>
				<quest event="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY"/>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Continue...</text>
					<event/>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
		<choice hidden="true" req="leah_nemesis_leah_quest_relay" lvl="2" max_lvl="2" blue="false">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"Hey, beyatch! These people have no decency, raising their shields like that. That's like my only weakness! What's a gal gotta do to Beam her enemy ship without a dumb shield getting in the way? Anyways, here are the coordinates to our next meeting point."
"One more pass. Just you wait beyatch, I'll get a beacon where no one attacks me eventually!" And with that, her ship's FTL Drive activates. With nothing else to do, you scrap the remains of the abandoned ship.</text>
				<instantEscape/>
				<autoReward level="MED">standard</autoReward>
				<quest event="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY"/>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Continue...</text>
					<event/>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
		<choice hidden="true" req="leah_nemesis_leah_quest_relay" lvl="3" max_lvl="3" blue="false">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"Hey, beyatch! We're over halfway there! I've picked up a few beams, I'll let you have one as a celebration. Not for free, beyatch, of course! Anyways, here are the coordinates to our next meeting point."
Once you're done browsing, her ship's FTL Drive activates. With nothing else to do, you scrap the abundant remains of the smoothly cut ship.</text>
				<instantEscape/>
				<autoReward level="HIGH">standard</autoReward>
				<quest event="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY"/>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Browse the Beam Master's store.</text>
					<event>
						<store>LEAH_STORE_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST</store>
					</event>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
		<choice hidden="true" req="leah_nemesis_leah_quest_relay" lvl="4" max_lvl="4" blue="false">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"Hey, beyatch! These enemy ships are getting rough. An expert like me knows how to get her Beams past shields, but for someone like you beyatch, you could totally have trouble using your beams against their 3 or 4 layers of shields! Anyways, here are the coordinates to our next meeting point."
And with that, her ship's FTL Drive activates. With nothing else to do, you scrap the abundant remains of the smoothly cut ship.</text>
				<instantEscape/>
				<autoReward level="HIGH">standard</autoReward>
				<quest event="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY"/>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Continue...</text>
					<event/>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
		<choice hidden="true" req="leah_nemesis_leah_quest_relay" lvl="5" max_lvl="5" blue="false">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"Hey, beyatch! Here are the coordinates to the last meeting point. It was a long journey, huh? Well, atleast it must have felt like one for you, beyatch! For me, it was as easy as a Voulge Beam cutting through your ship with no shields!"
"Speaking of the Voulge, I can't wait to see what beams they have in stock! My favourite is the Dirk, you know. There's a bit of debate about whether to count pinpoints as beams, but I can't help but like the little thing. Personally speaking, though, you can't go wrong with the classics, like the Glaive and the Voulge. And, get this, I've heard a rumour that there's something beyond the Voulge. Something POWERFUL."
"I've asked our dealer to check it out. If it's true, I call first dibs, beyatch!"
She transfers over the coordinates, and after ending her chatter, her ship's FTL Drive activates. With nothing else to do, you scrap the abundant remains of the smoothly cut ship.</text>
				<instantEscape/>
				<autoReward level="HIGH">standard</autoReward>
				<quest event="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY_FINAL"/>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Continue...</text>
					<event/>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
	</event>
	
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_RELAY_FINAL">
		<quest>
			<nebulaBeacon>true</nebulaBeacon>
			<currentSector>false</currentSector>
			<nextSector>true</nextSector>
			<sectorEight>true</sectorEight>
			<lastStand>true</lastStand>
		</quest>
		<preventQuest/>
		<preventFleet/>
		<preventBossFleet forever="true"/>
		<beaconType id="leah_nemesis_relay_final" global="true">
			<color r="255" g="200" b="0" a="1.0"/>
			<unvisitedTooltip>This is the location of the coordinates given to you by the "BEAM MASTER".</unvisitedTooltip>
			<visitedTooltip>Explored location. Nothing left of interest.</visitedTooltip>
		</beaconType>
		<text>You've arrived at the coordinates the "BEAM MASTER" gave. You see her familiar ship first, rather small and armed with Beam weapons. And then you see another familiar ship, larger and intimidating, painted with the distinct colours of a traveling merchant you know all too well.</text>
		<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS"/>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"Hey, beyatch! I've been waiting for you! This is our Beam dealer, he's kinda a weirdo, but he's got everything in stock!" You look at Sylvan, who merely chuckles in response.
"He's even got that mysterious beam I told you about! You know, the one larger and more powerful than the Voulge? I couldn't wait, I've already bought it! I can't wait to test it out! Don't worry beyatch, he had two in stock! It's almost like it was destiny for us two rivals to each have one, just like we were destined to be rivals!" She then pulls you aside for a private talk.

"Hey, beyatch, thanks for going along with me and sticking around. After all those times of you pretending not to know me, and destroying my ship without even acknowledging me, I'm glad you could finally appreciate our rivalry. And I know we're rivals and all, but it was... nice to have something else to look forward to, other than killing you. Bleh. Don't make me say it again, beyatch. Anyways, as a token and a gesture of my appreciation, I won't immediately flail you with my new beam! Ahahaha! I'm just kidding, here's your actual reward. A bundle of scrap I've Beamed up and am lending to you, and a secret for later! Buy a Beam for yourself, and even if you don't want to, do it for me, for our inevitable rivalry when we meet again!"

And with that, the Beam Master jumps away for the last time, leaving you utterly confused as to who that was.</text>
				<item_modify>
					<item type="scrap" min="99" max="99"/>
				</item_modify>
				<metaVariable name="leah_prof_nemesis_leah_quest_completed" op="set" val="1"/>
				<instantEscape/>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Browse the Traveling Merchant's Beam store</text>
					<event>
						<store>LEAH_STORE_NEMESIS_LEAH_QUEST_FINAL</store>
					</event>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
	</event>

	<mod:findName type="event" name="NEMESIS_ENCOUNTER">
		<mod-append:choice req="LIST_CREW_LEAH" max_group="666" hidden="true" blue="true">
			<text>(Leah) Use Leah to hail the ship.</text>
			<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH"/>
		</mod-append:choice>
	</mod:findName>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH">
		<loadEventList seeded="true" generate="true">
			<event name="LEAH_LIST_NEMESIS_LEAH"/>
		</loadEventList>
	</event>
	<eventList name="LEAH_LIST_NEMESIS_LEAH">
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_MIMIC"/>
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO"/>
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_CREW"/>
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_CREW"/>
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WEAPON"/>
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WEAPON"/>
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SCRAP"/>
		<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_SCRAP"/>
	</eventList>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_MIMIC" unique="true">
		<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
		<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of m-", She stops suddenly. Both Leahs push you out of the room. The door shuts behind you. You hear no noise, only silence.</text>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Open the door.</text>
			<event>
				<text>Leah is standing in the middle of the room. She stares at you, unblinking, silent, with an unnatural smile on her face. The other Leah is nowhere to be found.</text>
				<choice>
					<text>Trade. Leah. Offer. Sacrifice. Beam. Special. Stock.</text>
					<event>
						<text>ACCORD. MADE.</text>
						<metaVariable name="prof_leah_deaths" op="add" val="1"/>
						<variable name="loc_nemesis" op="set" val="1"/>
						<removeCrew class="unique_leah">
							<clone>false</clone>
							<text/>
						</removeCrew>
						<weapon name="LEAH_LIST_WEAPONS_BEAM_SPECIAL"/>
						<ship hostile="false"/>
						<choice hidden="true">
							<text>Continue...</text>
							<event/>
						</choice>
					</event>
				</choice>
				<choice>
					<text>NO NO NO NO NO NO.</text>
					<event>
						<text>You blink and suddenly the other Leah is there, clutching a hand to her chest.
					
"Damn you, Federation scum! This isn't the last you've seen of me! You beyatch and your little beyatch better watch your backs because I'm coming for you! Mwahahahah!"

She laughs before warping away. Evidently, your Leah won the fight!</text>
						<choice hidden="true">
							<text>Continue...</text>
							<event>
								<text>Without their leader, the rebel ship is easy pickings, and easy scrap.</text>
								<ship hostile="false"/>
								<weapon name="LOOT_KNIGHT_1"/>
								<metaVariable name="prof_leah_deaths" op="add" val="1"/>
								<variable name="loc_nemesis" op="set" val="1"/>
								<choice>
									<text>Continue...</text>
									<event/>
								</choice>
							</event>
						</choice>
					</event>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO" unique="true">
		<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
		<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of me on your ship!?" is what you think she is trying to say, but its hard to tell over the shouting of Leah, who is also next to you.
"I didn't replace YOU with a copy of yourself, who the HELL do you think you are!?",
"Don't try to invade on MY rival, beyatch, I've had to endure days of poor cruiser management, and there's no way I'm going to lose my rival for something like this!", is what you hear before swiftly retreating out of the room.

The muffled shouting leaks through the door, until eventually, it stops. Both Leahs come out, worse for the wear.

"Beyatch, I'm your rival, ditch this beyatch so we can get on with our rivalry!"</text>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>"I'm the real Leah, beyatch!", "No, beyatch, I'm the real Leah, beyatch!", "Ugh! We'll never end this if you keep lying like that, beyatch!",
				
"Wait! I know! Beyatch, remember that time you shut off my ship with an EMP field using that shield generator's reactor? Now you know she's the beyatch!", "Oh come on, Delta-Base 9T-83, that one is public information! Beyatch, remember when I bought all those missiles but forgot to buy ammo for them? Now that's something the beyatch would never know!"
				
"Yeah, and your drones as well!", Leah rolls her eyes. "The Lanius! Remember when they dismantled my ship's oxygen and then I told you to help me and you did, but you also destroyed my ship in the process, you beyatch?!", "The Swarmlands! I remember bringing the Lanius from the Swarmlands! I also remember telling you to kill yourself, why didn't you listen to me, beyatch? We wouldn't be having this problem if you had!"

Both Leahs recount various adventures that you don't remember, from stories about Prodigy 43-A to failures in hacking an ASB. Ditching all her weapons for hacking, for 'advanced boarding drones', investing in 'fake mind reading', exactly 22 spiders (you killed them all, you monster beyatch!), accidental FTL drives, encounters with her 'bestie' Jerry, the list goes on and on.</text>
				<choice hidden="true">
					<text>Continue...</text>
					<event>
						<text>"Even that time in Chaos mode where you tried to cheat through console commands by inputting my NEMESIS_ENCOUNTER_CHAOS event, haha, I bet you never thought it would just lead to the same old fight, beyatch!"</text>
						<choice hidden="true">
							<text>Wait, what?</text>
							<event>
								<text>"Oh, for beyatch sake! Remember that time you flirted with me, showing me your big ass Beam! You told me you were madly in love with me! I know I said it would never work out, and it still won't, but I'll make a concession and call you my best (and only) rival! So declare me as your one and only rival and get rid of this beyatch!"

"What!? I would never bring that up willingly! Its an affront to our rivalry! That's how you know she's the beyatch! Declare ME as your one and only rival and get rid of this beyatch!"

Both Leahs implore you. It seems you must choose the right one.</text>
								<choice hidden="true">
									<text>Shoot Leah.</text>
									<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO_CONCLUSION"/>
								</choice>
								<choice hidden="true">
									<text>Shoot Leah.</text>
									<event load="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO_CONCLUSION"/>
								</choice>
							</event>
						</choice>
					</event>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WHO_IS_WHO_CONCLUSION" unique="true">
		<text>"Gah... You'll pay for this, Federation scum! Our rivalry is not over, will never, ever be over! Not in a million, a billion, a BEYATCH-ILLION years!"

Clutching a hand to her chest, Leah warps away. Without their leader, the rebel ship is easy pickings, and easy scrap.</text>
		<metaVariable name="prof_leah_deaths" op="add" val="1"/>
		<variable name="loc_nemesis" op="set" val="1"/>
		<ship hostile="false"/>
		<autoReward level="MED">leah_reward_special</autoReward>
		<weapon name="BEAM_1"/>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event/>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_CREW" unique="true">
		<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
		<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of me on your ship!?" is what you think she is trying to say, but its hard to tell over the shouting of Leah, who is also next to you.
"I didn't replace YOU with a copy of yourself, who the HELL do you think you are!?",
"Don't try to invade on MY rival, beyatch, I've had to endure days of poor cruiser management, and there's no way I'm going to lose my rival for something like this!", is what you hear before swiftly retreating out of the room.

The muffled shouting leaks through the door, until eventually, it stops. Both Leahs come out, worse for the wear.

"Beyatch, in my infinite wisdom, I've decided to join your ship! You clearly need the help, and there's no way you can beat me while you're suffering from your.. mental issues. I know, I know, you must have missed our rivalry every hour, but an exact lookalike of me?" She shakes her head. "Shut up, beyatch, and give me access to the storage hold! We've got beams to buy, beyatch!"</text>
		<crewMember amount="1" class="unique_leah" all_skills="0">Leah</crewMember>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Continue...</text>
			<event>
				<text>The rebels say a tearful (?) goodbye to their leader, but not before presenting her with a gift of some scrap!</text>
				<ship hostile="false"/>
				<autoReward level="LOW">leah_reward_special</autoReward>
				<choice>
					<text>Continue...</text>
					<event/>
				</choice>
			</event>
		</choice>
	</event>
	<event name="LEAH_NEMESIS_LEAH_WEAPON" unique="true">
		<ship load="SHIP_NEMESIS" hostile="true"/>
		<text>The captain hails you, revealing themselves to have obnoxiously bright blue hair and a smug glare. "Didn't expect to see m- wait, WHAT!? That's me!? I'm on your ship, but I haven't even teleported over yet!" The rebel ship's communications go blank, but then you hear a 'FWOOP' as their captain teleports onto your ship. Right next to you, in fact.

"WHAT THE HELL, BEYATCH!? WHY do you have a copy of me on your ship!?" is what you think she is trying to say, but its hard to tell over the shouting of Leah, who is also next to you. Its hard to tell which one instigated the fight, but before you know it, they're swinging at each other. They both teleport away, and you hear a commotion somewhere else on the ship. And another, elsewhere. And then another.

Apparently, their fight is happening all over the ship. Even if you wanted to, its nigh impossible to interfere: the moment you turn towards them, they've already teleported somewhere else. One of the Leahs eventually acquiesces, clutching a hand to her chest.

"Damn you, Federation scum! This isn't the last you've seen of me! You beyatch and your little beyatch better watch your backs because I'm coming for you! Mwahahahah!"

She laughs before warping away. Evidently, your Leah won the fight!</text>
